; Empty xs is fold's identity case: no body iteration runs, and the
; form's value is the evaluated `init`. This is the left-fold
; identity and the load-bearing case for "init is always evaluated,
; even when xs is empty." On the binary path it also exercises the
; `fold_capture_init` bridge's early-return: setup pops init from
; the captured field, sees xs.len == 0, and pushes init as the
; final value without scheduling any iter frames.
(fold [acc x] 42 [] (+ acc x))
